1","description":"The th in \'think\'","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-78ae-81f3-28703ed32192","description":"The ch in \'cheese\'","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7aad-9cd9-61b34de18fc0","description":"The j in \'juice\'","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-71cb-a845-491346c50905","description":"The t in \'train\'","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7027-a890-f5cd578cfb1b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the meaning of the name of the constellation Cygnus?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cygnus is Latin for swan. Its bright stars also form the Northern Cross, a prominent asterism.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-75d1-bba6-5058a2fe4dc7","description":"Swan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7381-8501-780aff7939aa","description":"Ring","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-75a9-a336-8890defa6e30","description":"River","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7088-9ceb-0477f72bece7","description":"Mountain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7dc8-b2ed-8fe8141695d4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"Although the Poodle is widely associated with France, in which country is it believed to have originated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Poodle\u2019s name is linked to the word \u201cPudel,\u201d referring to splashing in water; the breed was developed as a water retriever.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-76d6-bcce-316f2d15922e","description":"Germany","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-797e-b467-5cbfe1ee3eda","description":"Egypt","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7344-a674-91718ed707e7","description":"India","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-79ef-afd1-a1a6b5a7df73","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-73b9-9b80-aa65ffa8f3c7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was built by CERN near Geneva?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"CERN\u2019s Large Hadron Collider lies beneath the French-Swiss border and lets scientists study matter through high-energy collisions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7121-83ec-e3a7176a0435","description":"Particle accelerator","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7f64-93f9-ee050eb9a05c","description":"Art museum","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-756c-bac2-dd3821acdbc3","description":"Colossus computer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7f66-9808-221b1b231f84","description":"Rocket launch pad","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-71eb-8918-cb998945c614","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was Rubik\'s Cube originally called when Ern\u0151 Rubik invented it in 1974?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Magic Cube was developed as a teaching tool for three-dimensional geometry before it was marketed internationally under Rubik\u2019s name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-72bf-8312-8689171899ab","description":"Magic Cube","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-71a7-aa8b-a6576b80ab48","description":"Wonder Cube","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7d4c-a5bb-35cbe654cb7f","description":"Hungarian Box","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-78d0-b742-42229947d689","description":"Colour Block","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7627-b84f-6ee00a918452","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"According to the biblical story of Cain and Abel, what type of animals did Abel offer as a sacrifice to God?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Genesis says Abel brought the firstborn of his flock as an offering, identifying the animals as sheep.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-75de-a996-8cff6aa03093","description":"Sheep","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7b17-9630-4202e4aa659a","description":"Cows","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-36cb-7cdb-9b6d-431